course: dictionary
lesson: 5496
title: A polite word for the toilet
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A lavatory is a toilet: the bowl you use to get rid of waste from your body. It can also mean the room, or small building, that holds a toilet. «"Lavatory" is a polite, old word for the toilet.» That is why you will often see it on signs in planes, trains and public buildings.
explain: Words for the same thing can sound very different. People in the UK might say «loo» (informal), people in the US might say «restroom» or «bathroom», and people in Australia might say «dunny» (slang). «Lavatory» is more polite and a little formal, so it sounds right on a sign or in a polite conversation.
explain: Context helps you see which word fits. A sign that says «Lavatory this way» tells you where the toilet is, and a polite voice asking «Where is the lavatory, please?» tells you the speaker wants to be polite, not joking. Check the clues around the word to see how formal or relaxed it is.
fact: A lavatory is a toilet, or a room or small building with a toilet in it.
fact: «Lavatory» is a polite and slightly formal or old-fashioned word.
fact: «Loo» is an informal word for the toilet, used mainly in the UK.
fact: «Dunny» is slang for the toilet, used in Australia.
fact: For the toilet, people pick a polite name («lavatory»), a sailor's word («the head») or a joke («the smallest room»).
exercise: You see a sign on a plane that says «Lavatory». What does lavatory mean here? | A small bag for luggage | A seat with a belt | A kitchen for making food | *A toilet
exercise: Which word is the most polite way to name the toilet? | loo | dunny | *lavatory | the smallest room
exercise: In Australia people may say «dunny». What kind of word is it? | A word that means a bath | *Slang | A sailor's word | Polite and formal
test: Which name for the toilet is a joke? | the head | *the smallest room | loo | lavatory
test: Which word would be most polite on a sign in a public building? | *lavatory | the smallest room | the head | dunny
exam: «"Lavatory" is a polite, old word for the toilet.» Why might a sign in a plane say lavatory instead of loo? | Because loo is the only correct word | Because it is a Scottish word | Because lavatory means a bath | *Because it is more polite and a little formal
